"Design (2026-08-12, user): IMPROVISED PICKUP BY SIZE DELTA. Any sufficiently small decoration (by size delta vs the taker) can be picked up, thrown, or used to bash. Implications: (1) the takeable/decoration distinction DISSOLVES -- takeability becomes a SIZE COMPARISON against the taker rather than an ItemComponent privilege; decorations get sizes (the size stat on their stat context), and take validates size delta. A human pockets a rock; a giant pockets a boulder; a fairy pockets a pebble and can carry none of the above. (2) Thrown/bash on a picked-up decoration = the IMPROVISED armament space from the original loadout design: a held decoration provides improvised properties (blunt-ish, magnitude scaled by ITS size relative to the wielder -- the magnitude-scaling-in-improvised-space note), granting throw/bash improvised actions. (3) This also closes the loop with attackable scenery (player-attack-while-exploring) and the size design notes: pick up the brazier or be too small to. ItemComponent remains for CRAFTED gear (armament/armor/relic asset refs); improvised carry is the size-gated general case layered on containment. Not implemented; depends on entities carrying the size stat + take validation gaining the size-delta check."